            <ArticleTitle>Allergy to macadamia nut.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Nuts are one of the most common foods causing allergic reactions in children and adults although an allergic reaction to macadamia nut has been reported only once previously.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a case of macadamia nut-induced allergic reaction.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Skin prick test with macadamia nut was performed in a private practice office.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The results demonstrated type-I hypersensitivity reaction with macadamia nut.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Macadamia nut ingestion can cause immediate-type allergic reactions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
